menu "DS18x20"

	choice DS18X20_ONEWIRE_BACKEND
		prompt "1-Wire backend"
		default DS18X20_ONEWIRE_BACKEND_BITBANG
		help
			The driver needs a 1-Wire bus implementation. Two of them are
			available: the bit-banging driver of esp-idf-lib and the RMT
			driver of Espressif (component espressif/onewire_bus).

			The bit-banging driver does not use any peripheral, but it
			keeps the interrupts disabled while a byte is transferred.
			The RMT driver runs in the background, so it tolerates long
			interrupt latencies better, but it occupies a pair of RMT
			channels.

		config DS18X20_ONEWIRE_BACKEND_BITBANG
			bool "esp-idf-lib bit-banging driver"
		config DS18X20_ONEWIRE_BACKEND_ESPRESSIF
			bool "espressif/onewire_bus (RMT)"
	endchoice

	config DS18X20_MAX_BUSES
		int "Maximum number of 1-Wire buses"
		depends on DS18X20_ONEWIRE_BACKEND_ESPRESSIF
		range 1 8
		default 4
		help
			The RMT backend needs a bus object for every GPIO pin the driver
			is used with. The objects are created on the first access to the
			pin and are kept until ds18x20_bus_free() is called. Note that
			every bus occupies a pair of RMT channels.

endmenu
